cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "colombian-open-data-mcp: an MCP server for Colombia's open government data"
message: >-
  If you use this software, or figures obtained through it, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alberto
    family-names: Castillo Aroca
    alias: alcastaro
    affiliation: >-
      OLDS — Observatorio Latinoamericano de Desarrollo Sostenible
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/alcastaro/colombian-open-data-mcp"
url: "https://github.com/alcastaro/colombian-open-data-mcp"
abstract: >-
  A Model Context Protocol server that turns Colombia's open government data
  into a native integration for any MCP client. It covers five portals: the
  national catalogue at datos.gov.co, which runs Socrata and is queried
  server-side with SoQL, and the territorial catalogues of Bogotá, Cali, Valle
  del Cauca and Cartagena, which run CKAN and are queried through the
  DataStore. Where a territorial dataset is not in the DataStore, the server
  reaches it two other ways: through the ArcGIS REST services many are
  published as, which filter and aggregate remotely, and by reading the
  published file. Nothing is cached and nothing is stored. The differences
  between the platforms are exposed rather than smoothed over: no CKAN portal
  offers server-side aggregation over its DataStore, and the server declines to
  advertise one.
